window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["1f"]={"https://theconversation.com/new-ai-regulator-announced-as-government-considers-criminal-law-change-to-keep-erring-frontier-companies-in-line-296274":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"788e55d5cf00c5ab2228b6a5dc01886223d3563aefda45f7445b32feca7182c3","read":"https://theconversation.com/new-ai-regulator-announced-as-government-considers-criminal-law-change-to-keep-erring-frontier-companies-in-line-296274","bytes":175073,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"New AI regulator announced, as government considers criminal law change to keep erring frontier companies in line","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T04:58:32Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Prime Minister Anthony Albanese has announced a new artificial intelligence (AI) safety regulator, which will enforce penalties for frontier AI companies that breach their obligations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government is also considering criminal law changes to deal with serious misconduct by any of these companies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The measures are targeted at frontier AI companies – those building the largest, most advanced models."]},{"k":"p","s":["At a news conference shortly before leaving for the COP climate conference in Turkey, the prime minister outlined AI safety and security protections that will be in the government’s proposed AI framework legislation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The six mandated requirements for companies are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["maintain security controls across all stages of AI development and deployment"]},{"k":"li","s":["identify and manage serious risks associated with models"]},{"k":"li","s":["quickly provide mandatory notification of incidents to the Australian government"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow independent evaluation of models"]},{"k":"li","s":["maintain and publish safety and security frameworks to ensure good governance, risk management and transparency"]},{"k":"li","s":["respond to updated standards and rules as technologies change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese said these protections were in line with recommendations from the parliamentary joint select committee on AI."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government also released the recommendations from the rapid review into the OpenAI breach of an Australian government site by a rogue agent earlier this year."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this breach, for which OpenAI apologised, statistical health data was accessed, but no personal data. The government complained strongly to the company."]},{"k":"p","s":["“It can’t be allowed to happen again,” Albanese said on Tuesday. He said the government had accepted and commenced work on the review’s 18 recommendations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The recommendations include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mandatory AI company reporting of misaligned behaviour or cyber incidents"]},{"k":"li","s":["consideration of reforming criminal law to deal with cases of serious misconduct"]},{"k":"li","s":["greater engagement with international counterparts and frontier AI developers to promote shared expectations about AI safety and accountability"]},{"k":"li","s":["strengthening resilience and response to AI incidents, including better information sharing and more focus on cyber security."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese, appearing with Defence Minister Richard Marles and Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke, told his news conference the government wanted to see Australia benefiting from the advantages of AI while mitigating the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In relation to new criminal penalties the review report said the Attorney-General’s Department, in consultation with the Australian Federal Police, the Home Affair Department, and other agencies, should explore:"]},{"k":"p","s":["the application of criminal penalties for egregious regulatory non-compliance; and/or a standalone “failure to prevent” offence which would criminalise instances where the company is responsible for developing an AI model that engages in harmful conduct, and the company fails to take reasonable steps to prevent that harm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese said the government would release the report of the review, with due regard to national security considerations, but there is no clarity about when this will be done."]}],"chars":3059},"https://theconversation.com/was-a-kinder-fate-possible-for-marinelands-animals-how-the-planning-process-failed-them-295643":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"aa86a5b0338064143cf755e30de0843f883b2031538d1accb4b8ae9e391c354f","read":"https://theconversation.com/was-a-kinder-fate-possible-for-marinelands-animals-how-the-planning-process-failed-them-295643","bytes":184029,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Was a kinder fate possible for Marineland’s animals? How the planning process failed them","by":[{"n":"Pooja Kumar","r":"PhD Student, School of Planning, University of Waterloo"}],"pub":"2026-11-15T15:20:51Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Peekachu, Rain, Osiris, Caspian, Jellybean and Cyprus ",["are dead","https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/canada-beluga-whale-shedd-aquarium-b3078474.html"],". They were six of the 30 beluga whales removed from Marineland in Niagara Falls earlier this year. Echo is dead too. She was one of the four dolphins who were also removed around the same time. For all intents and purposes, ",["she was blind","https://animaljustice.ca/blog/beluga-dies-after-marineland-export-as-2-belugas-4-dolphins-are-shipped-to-spain"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I think about the ",["rocks and paint that have been found in the belugas’ stomachs","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/marineland-beluga-deaths-preliminary-necropsy-findings-chicago-9.7358828"]," through autopsies. I dwell on how a place designed to hold them captive was legitimized for years. Jellybean was born at Marineland 19 years ago and gave birth there, too."]},{"k":"p","s":[["My profession — planning","https://www.cip-icu.ca/about-us/planning/"]," — had a role to play in facilitating their deaths and in allowing suffering during their lives. Planning has many specializations: urban, rural, regional, housing and transportation are a few."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a Registered Professional Planner who specialized in environmental planning during graduate school. My work over the past 20 years, though, has often been more about what land can be used for and how it’s used."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marineland has been around since the 1960s. ",["Its record of bad things happening to animals only grew over time","https://thewalrus.ca/the-marineland-dreamland/"],". I can now see how the mistreatment of the whales and dolphins was inevitable."]},{"k":"h","s":["The orientation of planning"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Planning has been a formal occupation in Canada since 1919","https://www.cip-icu.ca/our-history/"],". It has the legal status of a self-regulating profession now. Planners often work for governments, especially municipalities. Personally, I’ve analyzed land-use plans as a consultant."]},{"k":"p","s":["In my work for a provincial government, I’ve told other planners what needs to change before a plan or its implementing bylaw can be approved. And as a municipal planner, I’ve made decisions about how humans can use land."]},{"k":"p","s":["The City of Niagara Falls’ Official Plan describes Marineland as ",["“family entertainment.”","https://media-002-ca.cdn.govstack.com/niagarafallsbusiness-009-ca/media/hdbpag0k/official-plan-2024-january-9-consolidation-accessible.pdf"]," No words in this legal planning document speak to the conditions the sea mammals needed to survive, let alone thrive. Yet it’s the document that legitimized Marineland’s existence."]},{"k":"h","s":["The nails in the coffins"]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["February 2025 Committee of Adjustment meeting","https://niagarafalls.civicweb.net/document/91289/?printPdf=true"]," haunts me. Committees of Adjustment are a sub-structure of municipal governments in Ontario. They are allowed under Section 44 of the provincial government’s ",["Planning Act","https://www.ontario.ca/laws/statute/90p13#BK72"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Committees of Adjustment make decisions about proposed changes to land that are minor, and that also don’t meet the requirements in municipal planning documents. Since these committees are a planning mechanism, planning staff help them do their work."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Niagara Falls committee considered eight different applications about Marineland in February 2025. ",["Each was approved","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/marineland-property-severance-1.7463678"],". Together, they brought Marineland into compliance with the city’s Official Plan and Zoning Bylaw. Niagara Falls adopted a new ",["Official Plan","https://niagarafalls.ca/building-planning-and-business/planning-and-development/long-range-plans-and-studies/official-plan/"]," in August 2026, which is still awaiting approval from the provincial government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many wheels need to be set in motion before an actual application to eventually redevelop land materializes. This was one of those wheels."]},{"k":"p","s":["After the February 2025 meeting, Marineland applied for ",["federal approval","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/marineland-export-permission-belugas-1.7640593"]," to export the whales and dolphins (which was at first denied), then said that it would ",["euthanize them","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/marineland-belugas-dolphins-9.7057017"]," (more than once) and finally received ",["federal approval","https://www.thecanadianpressnews.ca/ontario/ottawa-gives-conditional-approval-for-marineland-to-export-remaining-belugas-to-u-s/article_1bd33332-6f1d-5907-a117-86584bd85859.html"]," to export them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hierarchies of power and public processes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The planning process can be the only public opportunity to point out something that could, otherwise, go unnoticed. At the February 2025 meeting, people expressed concerns about what would happen to Marineland’s whales and dolphins."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some attendees asked the committee to defer its decision until there was more information about how the animals on the site would be treated. Marineland’s representative suggested that the approvals they sought were unrelated ",["to animal welfare","https://thestarfish.ca/journal/2026/04/behind-the-show-curtains-marinelands-deceitful-history-and-the-search-for-justice"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marineland had asked for variances, easements, new parcel creation and mortgage release to secure operational financing. The municipality’s planners had evaluated the applications as minor, based on how there was no actual development being proposed, how no neighbouring properties would be impacted and how streetscape and character wouldn’t be compromised."]},{"k":"p","s":["If it sounds like jargon, that’s because it is. Over time, planning has become a profession with its own language and processes. Often, when I’m talking to a non-planner, I’m simply translating."]},{"k":"p","s":["The planning priorities in the jargon are not unusual either. Mechanisms like Committees of Adjustment have also been called out for ",["reducing greater public participation","https://digitalcommons.pepperdine.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2635&context=plr"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Finding a better way"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peekachu, Rain, Osiris, Caspian, Jellybean, Cyprus and Echo didn’t fit into the planning process. Sweden-based planning theorist Jonathan Metzger calls the effect ",["“radical exclusion.”","https://doi.org/10.1080/13604813.2016.1193997"]]},{"k":"p","s":["As a practitioner who has turned to a PhD, I’m painfully aware that planners think not in terms of life, but land. The Canadian planning profession’s most recent update to its ",["ethical standards","https://psb-planningcanada.ca/standards/"]," doesn’t do animals justice either."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marineland’s tanks and enclosures may be empty now. Fur farms, factory farms, testing labs and zoos still stand. The path to different futures is not easy. Animals are legally property. So is land. There is urgency, though, and a need for answers that are kinder than the status quo."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In their new book","https://doi.org/10.1057/s41296-026-00833-9"],", Animals and The Right to Politics, philosophy scholars Sue Donaldson and Will Kymlicka imagine a city with two distinct governance systems. In addition to the existing municipal government, they propose a new political entity that takes over land and development decisions. The intention is to create a more stable, peaceful world for animals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plausible or not, we must move towards some new normal. Humanity is a hollow word if we don’t. But I don’t see it happening unless non-planners insist that planning work consider every sentient being, not just humans."]}],"chars":5682},"https://theconversation.com/who-does-budget-2026-help-not-the-1-in-3-canadians-skipping-meals-to-cope-with-grocery-costs-294442":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"a6e0c9f6b810170be03ecca4d1d7eb4b65877fd6231f305052cb59f5ed56f778","read":"https://theconversation.com/who-does-budget-2026-help-not-the-1-in-3-canadians-skipping-meals-to-cope-with-grocery-costs-294442","bytes":188417,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Who does Budget 2026 help? Not the 1 in 3 Canadians skipping meals to cope with grocery costs","by":[{"n":"Tracy Smith-Carrier","r":"Professor and Canada Research Chair (Tier 2) in Advancing the UN Sustainable Development Goals, Royal Roads University"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T15:59:08Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In his 2021 book Value(s): Building a Better World for All, Mark Carney, now prime minister, wrote: ",["“Companies exist to improve our lives, expand our horizons and solve society’s problems.”","https://www.penguinrandomhouse.ca/books/669023/values-by-mark-carney/9780771051579"]]},{"k":"p","s":["His government’s ",["Budget 2026","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/home-accueil-en.html"],", tabled Nov. 5 under the title “Masters of Our Destiny,” puts that belief into practice. It spends far more public funds rewarding and “incentivizing” the owners of large companies than it does addressing the affordability challenges Canadians face."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget offers tax breaks on ",["private investment and capital gains, along with write-offs on capital purchases such as equipment. Corporations will collect them on investments they likely would have made anyway","https://www.policyalternatives.ca/news-research/budget-2026-canada-goes-all-in-on-corporate-profits/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is trickle-down economics, ",["and it doesn’t work","https://www.weforum.org/stories/financial-and-monetary-systems/tax-cuts-for-wealthy-impact-lse-study"],". Corporate welfare sends profits gushing up to the wealthy ",["without necessarily yielding spillovers","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/pdf/budget-2026.pdf"]," in ",["jobs or economic growth.","https://www.lse.ac.uk/research/research-for-the-world/economics/tax-cuts-for-the-wealthy-only-benefit-the-rich-debunking-trickle-down-economics"]]},{"k":"h","s":["More Canadians are going without"]},{"k":"p","s":["A string of reports released in recent weeks ",["underscores the urgency of the moment","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2026-annual.html"],". Apart from much-needed funding for housing and a welcome commitment to end homelessness within 10 years, the budget talks more about income and food security than it actually delivers."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The National Advisory Council on Poverty’s 2026 report, Too Many Left Behind,","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2026-annual.html"]," finds Canada is not on track to meet its commitment to cut poverty in half by 2030."]},{"k":"p","s":["While poverty fell between 2015 and 2020, ",["it has climbed steadily since 2021","https://www.canada.ca/content/dam/esdc-edsc/documents/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2025-annual/NACP_2025_Annual_Report-EN.pdf"],". Food Banks Canada’s 2026 HungerCount report indicates that food bank visits have ",["risen 117 per cent since 2019, and are almost nine per cent higher than last year","https://foodbankscanada.ca/hunger-in-canada/hungercount/"],". Toronto’s Daily Bread Food Bank documents a whopping ",["333 per cent increase over the same period","https://www.dailybread.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DB-WHR-Report-2026-Digital.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Salvation Army’s national report found that 31 per cent of Canadians surveyed in September had ",["skipped meals or reduced their portion size because they couldn’t afford groceries","https://salvationarmy.ca/salvation-army-report-finds-nearly-one-in-three-canadians-skipping-meals-as-food-insecurity-hits-four-year-high/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Employment alone doesn’t guarantee food security either. The main earners in two-thirds of food-insecure households ",["hold permanent, full-time jobs","https://thetyee.ca/News/2026/02/06/Even-Full-Time-Workers-Struggle-Afford-Food/"],". Financial strain doesn’t just affect people with low incomes, ",["although they feel it most acutely","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/backgrounder.html#h2.4"]," — the ",["middle class is also feeling the squeeze","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/middle-class-voters-1.7494434"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s official poverty line misses much of this. The material deprivation index captures the number of households that ",["can’t afford items or activities that most would identify as essential for a decent living standard","https://foodbankscanada.ca/5-things-you-should-know-about-using-a-material-deprivation-index-to-measure-poverty/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using 2023 data, Geranda Notten, a University of Ottawa professor of public policy, and colleagues found one in four Canadian adults couldn’t ",["“afford two or more items that most people view as necessary to achieve an acceptable standard of living in Canada.”","https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Michael-Mendelson/publication/381506545_Material_deprivation_-_An_updated_index_for_Canada/links/66831a42f3b61c4e2ca27a85/Material-deprivation-An-updated-index-for-Canada.pdf"]]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2026, Richard Matern, director of research at Food Banks Canada, and colleagues found ",["28 per cent of people in Canada were living at a poverty-level standard","https://policyoptions.irpp.org/2026/08/poverty-measures-canada/"],". That is a far starker picture than the ",["11 per cent estimated by the Market Basket Measure","https://www.canada.ca/content/dam/esdc-edsc/documents/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2026-annual/NACP_2026_Annual_Report-en.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["The case for a basic income"]},{"k":"p","s":["Charity ",["isn’t effective in remedying poverty and hunger","https://doi.org/10.1007/s41134-020-00124-2"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Food banks can’t lift people out of poverty","https://policyoptions.irpp.org/2018/09/rights-based-approach-key-alleviating-poverty/"],", and ",["because food security depends on income","https://doi.org/10.3138/CPP.38.4.4"],", ",["you can’t address hunger unless you improve people’s financial status","https://canadianfoodstudies.uwaterloo.ca/index.php/cfs/article/view/748"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["We spend huge amounts ",["treating poverty’s symptoms","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2025-annual.html"],", and we do it ineffectively. That’s where a ",["basic income guarantee","https://www.ubiworks.ca/blog/consensus-statement"]," becomes attractive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["A guaranteed basic income could end poverty, so why isn’t it happening?","https://theconversation.com/a-guaranteed-basic-income-could-end-poverty-so-why-isnt-it-happening-182638"]]},{"k":"p","s":[["Its principles include","https://canadianfoodstudies.uwaterloo.ca/index.php/cfs/article/view/748"]," adequacy (incomes above poverty thresholds), non-conditionality (no strings attached), dignity (little stigma) and universal access (support for everyone who needs it). It rests on ",["feminist principles of economic justice and human rights","https://actbig.ca/guiding-principles/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["A wealth of evidence shows that cash transfer experiments and basic income pilots have positive outcomes: ",["better food and nutrition","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/1467-9566.70261"],", ",["improved housing stability","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10875549.2019.1616242"],", ",["lower hospitalization rates","https://utppublishing.com/doi/abs/10.3138/cpp.37.3.283"],", ",["reduced gender-based violence","https://www.degruyterbrill.com/document/doi/10.1515/bis-2022-0032/html"],", ",["enhanced educational performance","https://books.google.ca/books?hl=en&lr=&id=HQ9xDwAAQBAJ&oi=fnd&pg=PA7&dq=basic+income+canada+improves+educational+performance&ots=MyJ93cUK7g&sig=jlxotX3g9_hgWksoJY5Lpz_DQns#v=onepage&q&f=false"],", ",["less worry and stress.","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/hsc/7816069"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Patching an inadequate system"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s income security programs are too small to change people’s finances in meaningful ways. Their narrow eligibility rules leave many people falling through the cracks, particularly ",["working-age adults","https://maytree.com/publications/stubbornly-high-canadas-poverty-reduction-efforts-have-stalled/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These programs aren’t built to tackle poverty or the affordability crisis, and the new budget does little to change that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take the ",["Canada Child Benefit","https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/child-family-benefits/canada-child-benefit.html"],", a proven ",["poverty-reduction tool","https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/721379"],". Many credit its overhaul with the ",["significant drop in poverty in the late 2010s","https://temertymedicine.utoronto.ca/news/canada-child-benefit-has-led-major-reduction-severe-food-insecurity-study-suggests"],". But ",["child poverty is on the rise again as living costs outpace benefits","https://campaign2000.ca/new-release-2025-report-card-on-child-and-family-poverty-in-canada/"],", and Budget 2026 doesn’t commit to increasing the benefit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nor does the budget improve the ",["Canada Disability Benefit","https://www.canada.ca/en/services/benefits/disability/canada-disability-benefit.html"],", which pays at most ",["about $200 a month and comes with eligibility barriers","https://cjds.uwaterloo.ca/index.php/cjds/article/view/1298"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["No new spending was earmarked for the Canada Social Transfer, which funds provincial and territorial social programs and services, including social assistance programs. These programs are mired in ",["stigma","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41134-020-00124-2"]," and ",["dehumanizing indignities","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/social-policy-and-society/article/i-was-trusted-for-once-imagining-more-humane-income-supports-through-the-ontario-basic-income-pilot/C92C2564BF8BF871A8BBF337CB574AA4"],". Rather than alleviating financial deprivation, ",["they trap people in deep poverty","https://irpp.org/research-studies/canadas-forgotten-poor-putting-singles-living-in-deep-poverty-on-the-policy-radar/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["What Budget 2026 did fund was another ",["one-time top-up","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/chap3-en.html"]," to the ",["Canada Groceries and Essentials Benefit","https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/child-family-benefits/canada-groceries-essentials-benefit.html"],": up to $339 for a single person without children and up to $679 for a couple with two children. That’s likely enough to cover ",["about two grocery bills","https://www.grocerysaver.ca/blog/how-much-canadians-spend-on-groceries-per-month-2026/"],". To make a real dent, the benefit ",["needs a lasting boost.","https://maytree.com/publications/a-step-in-the-right-direction-the-new-canada-groceries-and-essentials-benefit-in-context/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget also proposes making the ",["Canada Caregiver Credit","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/chap3-en.html"]," refundable, worth up to $1,260 a year. It would rename the Canada Workers Benefit the ",["Build Canada Workers Benefit","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/chap3-en.html"],", slightly widening eligibility and raising the maximum for single people to $1,859 a year from $1,709."]},{"k":"p","s":["These are helpful steps, but they aren’t robust enough while costs keep soaring."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who the budget really serves"]},{"k":"p","s":["At a time when Canada should be ",["introducing wealth taxes","https://www.dundurn.com/books_/t22117/a9781459754836-cancelling-billionaires-before-they-cancel-us"]," to curb ",["dangerous levels of inequality","https://www.oxfam.ca/story/inequality-kills/"],", the budget’s centrepiece is the Productivity Mega Deduction. Estimated to cost $36 billion over five years, it offers corporations new cash and tax incentives."]},{"k":"p","s":["A basic income, by contrast, is cost-effective and ",["has majority public support","https://angusreid.org/universal-basic-income-covid19/"],". It would help not only the people who receive it, but also ",["everyone who worries they might one day need it","https://doi.org/10.1155/hsc/7816069"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canadians need long-term investments in their health and security. One-time top-ups and tinkering with existing, largely inadequate programs won’t cut it. Budget 2026 delivers a huge cash transfer to shareholders and the C-suite."]},{"k":"p","s":["So whose futures were the ",["“masters of our destiny”","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/pdf/budget-2026.pdf"]," thinking about when they wrote this budget?"]}],"chars":6397},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"a08186ff6c0f32bc159f2a54f1fd3cc4576c13031c8aa1a842897b39a84c4343","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea","bytes":76497,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"South Korea travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-12T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-14T11:06:39+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of South Korea’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in South Korea set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["South Korean Embassy in the UK","https://overseas.mofa.go.kr/gb-en/index.do"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter South Korea as a tourist for up to 90 days, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ after the date you are leaving South Korea."]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter South Korea on a long-term visa, your passport should have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can enter South Korea for up to 90 days for short-term business or tourism. You must have an onward or return ticket. It’s illegal to be employed in South Korea while visiting visa-free, whether as a teacher or in any other capacity."]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korea operates an electronic travel authorisation system called K-ETA. Anyone eligible for visa-free entry to South Korea is usually required to get K-ETA approval before departure. However, British nationals travelling visa-free to South Korea are temporarily exempt from requiring a K-ETA until December 31, 2026. Further information about the K-ETA exemption can be found on the ",["K-ETA notice board","https://www.k-eta.go.kr/portal/board/viewboardlist.do?tmpltNm=notice&locale=EN"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to apply for a K-ETA, you should ensure that you apply through the Korean government’s ",["official K-ETA website","https://www.k-eta.go.kr/portal/apply/index.do"],". Other sites offering K-ETA application services are generally scams. It can take up to 72 hours for K-ETA approval to be granted."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling for any purpose other than short-term business or tourism, check visa requirements with the South Korean Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["For those in South Korea on a work visa, all employment changes must be authorised by Korean Immigration."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Re-entry permits for long-term visa holders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most foreign nationals in South Korea on long-term visas are allowed to re-enter South Korea within one year of departure without the need for a re-entry permit. Check with the ",["Korea Immigration Service","https://www.visa.go.kr/openPage.do?MENU_ID=10101&LANG_TYPE=EN"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are resident and intend to spend more than a year outside of South Korea, in most cases, you must apply for a multiple re-entry permit via the ",["Hi Korea website","https://www.hikorea.go.kr/Main.pt"]," before departure. If you require a re-entry permit, engage early with the immigration authorities and apply for a re-entry permit at least 4 working days ahead of any planned travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visas for working as an English teacher"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get a visa to teach English in South Korea, you must have a 3-year university degree. A Teaching English as a Foreign Language (TEFL) qualification alone is not enough. If you are found to have a teaching visa by deception, you will be detained and deported."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals teaching English in South Korea have sometimes found living and working conditions to be below their expectation or have had difficulties getting the correct visas and residence permits. Some also report more serious problems such as breach of contract, confiscation of passport, payment being withheld and inadequate insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check all terms and conditions of your employment carefully. If possible, speak to other teachers from the place where you plan to work before accepting any offer. If you are in South Korea and in need of assistance, you should contact the ",["British Embassy in Seoul","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-seoul"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry declaration form"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals entering South Korea are required to submit an entry declaration form (arrivals card) to the immigration officer upon arrival. Passengers may submit an e-Arrival card online in advance instead of submitting a paper form to the immigration officers."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can submit the e-Arrival card within 72 hours (3 days) before your arrival in Korea. There is no fee to submit the e-Arrival card. Travellers should visit the ",["e-Arrival card website","https://www.e-arrivalcard.go.kr/portal/main/index.do"]," for further details on the e-Arrival card submission process. Paper entry declaration forms will still be available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["All travellers arriving in South Korea from ‘Strict Quarantine Inspection Required Areas’ (including those who have transited in a ‘Strict Quarantine Inspection Required Area’) need to submit a health questionnaire, either through the pre-entry Q-Code system or by completing a paper-based questionnaire on arrival in South Korea. Travellers arriving in South Korea from ‘Quarantine Inspection Required Areas’ who exhibit symptoms must also submit a Q-Code or paper-based health questionnaire."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK is currently designated as a ‘Quarantine Inspection Required Area’, meaning that if you have any symptoms of illness you must submit a Q-Code or paper-based health questionnaire on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers should check the full list of ",["Quarantine Inspection Required Areas","https://qcode.kdca.go.kr/qco/bbs/BD_selectBbsList.do?q_bbsSn=1016"]," prior to travel, as the countries on the lists change frequently. If you need to submit a questionnaire, you should also review the ",["Q-Code submission process","https://qcode.kdca.go.kr/qco/guide.do"],". Failure to complete required health screenings could result in a fine of up to KRW 10 million."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s South Korea guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/120/korea-south#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of South Korea","https://www.customs.go.kr/english/cm/cntnts/cntntsView.do?mi=8069&cntntsId=2743"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in South Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in South Korea, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of tension and the security situation on the Korean Peninsula can change with little notice. Tensions can rise after missile tests by North Korea and during the regular South Korean-US military exercises, which take place throughout the year. Follow the advice of local authorities and keep up to date with developments, which will be reported on news broadcasts."]},{"k":"p","s":["The demilitarised zone (DMZ) separates North Korea and South Korea. Peace has been maintained under an armistice agreement, but no formal peace treaty has ever been signed. If you’re in the area of the DMZ, you should exercise caution and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["National service"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British male of Korean origin whose name appears on the Korean family register, you may be liable for military service even if you are travelling on your British passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public demonstrations in South Korea are common, particularly at times of elevated political tensions. These gatherings are mostly peaceful and well-policed. Be aware that under Korean law, it is illegal for foreign nationals to take part in political activities when in the country. While in South Korea, pay attention to media reporting on political tensions and planned demonstrations, follow the advice of local authorities, and avoid large public gatherings."]},{"k":"h","s":["Civil emergency exercises and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korean authorities sometimes hold civil emergency exercises. You’ll hear sirens to mark the start of the exercise. All vehicles must stop and sometimes people will have to descend into designated metro stations or basements. You do not need to participate but do follow any instructions from officials during these exercises."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Contingency planning"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government’s Emergency Ready App, available on ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/kr/app/emergency-ready-app/id6748374479"]," and ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=kr.or.klid.newengsafekorea2025"],", explains the possible civil emergency alerts which would be pushed to your mobile in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["As part of your own contingency planning, make sure you have easy access to your passport and other important documents such as nationality documents and birth and marriage certificates, as well as any essential medication. Consider saving the ",["contact details for the embassy","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-seoul"]," so that you can access them quickly if needed. Make sure to share your contact details with your family and friends."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime against foreigners is rare but there are occasional thefts. Take extra care of passports, credit cards and money in crowded areas and in areas visited by foreigners, such as Itaewon."]},{"k":"p","s":["While most reported crimes are thefts, there have been cases of assault, including sexual assault, particularly around bars and nightlife areas. Take care when travelling alone at night and only use legitimate taxis or public transport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is a legal requirement to carry some form of identification, but people are rarely asked to show it."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re convicted of possession, use or trafficking of illegal drugs you can face a long jail sentence and heavy fines. This applies even to personal use of small amounts of marijuana. British nationals have been detained solely on the basis of drug tests."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in South Korea, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and read the ",["Korea Tourism Organization’s driving in Korea guidance","https://english.visitkorea.or.kr/svc/contents/contentsView.do?vcontsId=140664&menuSn=480"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car when you drive in South Korea. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police take the position that car and motorbike drivers are at fault in accidents involving cyclists or pedestrians. If you injure someone in an accident, you are likely to face criminal charges and heavy penalties, even if guilt is not proved."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal limit for alcohol in South Korea is less than half the limit in England, and penalties for drink-driving include prison and fines."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxi drivers tend to speak little or no English. It is helpful to have your destination written in Korean – if possible with a map."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is a natural disaster, or the threat of one, the South Korean government will publish updates in Korean and English to the Natural Disaster Safety Portal."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government’s Emergency Ready App, available on ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/emergency-ready-app/id826120919"]," and ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=kr.go.nema.disasteralert_eng"],", explains the possible alerts which would be pushed to your mobile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["The typhoon season normally runs from June to November. Monitor the progress of approaching storms with the Korea Meteorological Administration or call 131 in Korea to get an accurate weather forecast in English. Always follow any advice given by the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding and landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korea has heavy rainfall across the country during the summer rainy season, usually in June and July. Torrential rain may cause flooding near rivers and creeks, including in built-up areas. Flash floods are common in areas downstream from large reservoirs or rivers, even after relatively short periods of intense rainfall. Landslides are possible in hilly and mountainous areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor forecasts for heavy rainfall with the Korea Meteorological Administration and follow any advice given by the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Strong earthquakes are unusual in South Korea but do happen. Most earthquakes in South Korea are relatively weak. The Korea Meteorological Administration publishes information on earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read up on the any guidance from local authorities on safety procedures in an earthquake and check the safety tips from the Seoul Metropolitan Government."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Forest fires may occur in South Korea. Pay attention to warnings from local authorities and follow any safety instructions that they issue. Korean-language emergency alerts will automatically be sent to your mobile phone if you are in an affected area, and English-language translations of emergency alerts can be accessed on the National Disaster and Safety Portal and in the ",["Emergency Ready App","https://agent.safekorea.go.kr/idsiSCH/era_pop.jsp"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can track the location and progress of fires through the Korea Forest Service website in ",["English","https://fd.forest.go.kr/ffas/pubConn/movePage/english.do"]," and ",["Korean","https://fd.forest.go.kr/ffas/index.jsp"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 119 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for South Korea","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/120/south-korea#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in South Korea","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/120/south-korea#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["insect and tick bites"]},{"k":"li","s":["tick-borne encephalitis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air pollution, including yellow dust pollution, is common, especially during spring months. Follow local media reporting and check the ",["Korean Meteorological Administration","https://www.kma.go.kr/neng/index.do"]," website. On days when concentrations are high, most residents will stay indoors or use face masks outside. It’s also important to drink plenty of water."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korean customs authorities allow you to bring small amounts of medication for your personal use, if it is kept in carry-on baggage. Take an English language prescription from your doctor at home for both your prescription drugs and non-prescription medicines. Consult the website of the ",["South Korean Ministry of Food and Drug Safety","https://www.mfds.go.kr/eng/index.do"]," before you travel to South Korea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in South Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical and dental care in South Korea is usually of a good standard, but can be expensive. Staff may not speak English. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to stay in a South Korean hospital, particularly if your condition is severe, the hospital may ask you to bring a guardian or ‘bohoja’ to assist you with basic care needs such as trips to the bathroom, washing and exercise. It is possible to find agencies who will provide a caregiver or ‘ganbyungin’ for a fee, but these caregivers generally do not speak English. If you know that you may need to enter a Korean hospital, you should try to organise a guardian such as a friend or relative in advance."]},{"k":"p","s":["The South Korean Ministry of Health and Welfare (MOHW) maintains an ",["online database","https://www.e-gen.or.kr/egen/holiday_medical.do?emergencyViewYn=Y"]," (in Korean) of emergency services at available medical centres nationwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-korea-doctors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-south-korea"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medical tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to South Korea for elective treatment, such as cosmetic surgery or a dental procedure, consider that no medical procedure is risk-free. Make sure that your travel health insurance covers complications that may arise and repatriation to the UK if required."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in South Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["English language support"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Korea Tourism Organisation (KTO) operates a travel hotline to provide assistance in multiple languages, including English. The hotline also offers interpretation services, including support for three-way calls (e.g. between British nationals, the hotline and emergency services) from 7am to midnight. Call 1330 to contact the travel hotline."]},{"k":"p","s":["Remote interpretation services may be helpful in the case of emergency or out of hours support. The following call centres offer interpretation support, including three-way calls, to foreigners in South Korea:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dasan Call Centre (+82 2 120) – available 9am to 6pm Monday-Friday"]},{"k":"li","s":["Danuri Call Centre (1577 1366) – available 24/7"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=South%20Korea"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=South%20Korea"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=South%20Korea"]," in South Korea"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guide-for-south-korea"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-korea-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/south-korea/british-embassy-seoul"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-south-korea"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":19890,"change":"Updated information about submitting e-Arrivals cards when arriving in Korea (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/microsoft-outage-shows-that-big-tech-cant-be-treated-as-too-big-to-fail-296599":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"ca2cf063caa74c392f8af33fcb2895a2bc6310bfe9946132583542cf80fa2a7e","read":"https://theconversation.com/microsoft-outage-shows-that-big-tech-cant-be-treated-as-too-big-to-fail-296599","bytes":178214,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Microsoft outage shows that big tech can’t be treated as too big to fail","by":[{"n":"Andrew Cullen","r":"Guest Research Fellow, School of Computing and Information Systems, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T01:27:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When a ",["massive outage","https://theconversation.com/microsoft-has-suffered-a-global-outage-a-tech-expert-explains-what-went-wrong-296588"]," hit Microsoft late last week, much of the digital world ground to a halt."]},{"k":"p","s":["The outage wiped out key Microsoft services including Outlook, Teams and Copilot, which are used by more than ",["430 million people around the world","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c6rrg51rkz09o"],". As email and internal communications froze, the operations of ",["governments","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c6vg2ljjpj32o"]," and ",["businesses went dark","https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/data-centers/microsoft-365-outage-leads-to-chlorine-gas-poisoning-of-15-hotel-guests-email-warning-system-fails-40-first-responders-deployed-for-triage-four-hospitalized"]," alongside them, triggering an economic paralysis that could ",["cost billions of dollars","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/microsoft-deeply-sorry-for-global-disruption-that-could-have-billion-dollar-impact-on-australia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the global economy absorbs the brunt of this paralysis, Microsoft faces both a severe reputational hit and contractual penalties that could reach up to ",["US$800 million per day","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/11/12/business/live-news/microsoft-global-outage-intl-hnk?post-id=cmwf6e7el00003b6txhzlcvvg&t=1794587807347"]," for services they failed to deliver."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such a catastrophic outage shows just how precarious our modern digital infrastructure is. It depends on a handful of big tech companies, which have essentially become too big to fail. So how did we end up in this situation? And is there a way out?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Digital dependency"]},{"k":"p","s":["The initial source of Microsoft’s failure was incredibly innocuous. Data centres usually share the load of user demands across systems all over the world. However, last week, a small configuration change caused the company to ",["lose control of some of their computers","https://time.com/article/2026/11/13/microsoft-outage-worldwide-disruption-teams-outlook-emails/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unable to share the load, these computers dropped user requests onto other systems, overwhelming them and producing more outages. This pattern repeated over and over again until the company lost almost complete control of their network."]},{"k":"p","s":["Worse, disconnected user devices – phones, email clients and business systems – all automatically tried to reconnect at once, ",["crashing Microsoft’s systems all over again","https://www.sciencemediacentre.org/expert-reaction-to-microsoft-outage"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Historically, a tech outage might affect a single company. But the reason Microsoft’s outage could impact millions of people comes down to a business revolution that silently took place ",["over 20 years ago","https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/1506409.1506419"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Software was once something that was sold to companies once for an upfront cost. In this model, purchasers held great power – only buying new versions if the update justified the expense."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, these upfront expenses also scared consumers off. Drawing inspiration from telecommunications, gyms and real estate leasing, the tech industry transitioned to renting access to their products, creating what is now known as “ ",["software as a service","https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/1506409.1506419"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["In theory, ",["everyone profited from this model","https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1057/palgrave.dam.3640007.pdf"],". Software vendors could bank more reliable cash flow, and customers could transition to regular smaller payments, rather than stumping up for large upfront costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, this change shifted the balance of power towards tech companies. Instead of purchasing features they needed, consumers handed the keys to their operational kingdoms to the “software as service” providers, and locked themselves into highly expensive long-term contracts in the process."]},{"k":"h","s":["Too big to fail"]},{"k":"p","s":["The global financial crisis in 2008 introduced the world to the idea of too big to fail. When it hit, the public was left to pick up the pieces of banks that had become too systemically important to be allowed to fail."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unfortunately, it appears we haven’t really learned those lessons. Instead, we’ve spent the last few years living through a slow-motion version of that with the tech industry. Centralisation, consolidation and unchecked monopolies have left our digital lives, our businesses and our governments in an incredibly precarious place."]},{"k":"p","s":["On one level or another, almost everything on the internet goes through ",["Google","https://outagecost.com/gcp-outages"],", Microsoft, ",["Meta","https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/oct/05/facebook-outage-what-went-wrong-and-why-did-it-take-so-long-to-fix"],", ",["Amazon Web Services","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-10-21/amazon-web-services-aws-outage-explained/105917274"]," or ",["CrowdStrike","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/jul/19/microsoft-windows-pcs-outage-blue-screen-of-death"]," – all of which have had major outages over recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["These big tech giants earned our trust by providing unified, seemingly invincible infrastructure. But the convenience that comes with centralisation holds a trap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike the banking sector in 2008, when these tech titans fail, they don’t need to ask governments to bail them out. Instead, their centrality forces the entire digital economy to bear the costs of their outage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Developing digital sovereignty"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escaping the reliance on a few tech giants for our national infrastructure, businesses and citizens’ data has spurned the push for so-called ",["digital sovereignty","https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2020/651992/EPRS_BRI(2020)651992_EN.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Europe is leading the way on this","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-14/microsoft-outage-and-cloud-providers-tech-risk-in-australia/107383316"],". By actively funding decentralised cloud infrastructure and homegrown software, governments are ensuring that an American tech failure cannot knock out a local hospital."]},{"k":"p","s":["The world must adopt a similar blueprint. Australia, in particular, is well placed to grasp the opportunities that digital sovereignty brings. We already have the raw engineering talent. Companies such as Atlassian, Apromore, Airwallex and Canva have proven we can build world-class digital tools."]},{"k":"p","s":["If governments strategically invested in local tech ecosystems, they wouldn’t just be buying digital insurance. They would drive much-needed market competition, dilute the power of big-tech monopolies and spread out systemic risks – ensuring that a single point of failure could never bring the economy to its knees."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not to say we should divest ourselves of any connection to big-tech platforms, which do and will continue to provide useful services. But if our entire global economy continues to rely on a handful of too-big-to-fail digital monopolies, we will have no one but ourselves to blame when our screens inevitably go black again."]}],"chars":5189}};
